  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>By IUPAC nomenclature,</p><p>The parent chain in this compound is the cyclohexane ring, which consists of six carbon atoms.</p><p>The substituents are:</p><p>Ethyl group  attached to third carbon.</p><p>Two methyl groups  attached to carbon <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> .</p><p>The Numbering must be given the carbons in the cyclohexane ring so that  the substituents get the lowest numbers,</p><p>Hence, the name is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>-ethyl <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo></math>-dimethylcyclohexane</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0127_cf96908dd9e0.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 201px;\"/></p>"
  }
